[
    {
        "content": "<p>Cool! How does it compare to <a href=\"https://github.com/WasmCert\">https://github.com/WasmCert</a><br>\nWe might be able to target that from <a href=\"https://peregrine-project.github.io/\">https://peregrine-project.github.io/</a></p>",
        "id": 597058931,
        "sender_full_name": "Bas Spitters",
        "timestamp": 1779470439
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/WasmCert\">https://github.com/WasmCert</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>WasmCert puts emphasis on verifying the WasmSpecification in Lean, and as I understand it the intention is to prove artifacts auto-generated from <a href=\"https://webassembly.org/news/2025-03-27-spectec/\">SpecTec</a>. Our focus is on proving the behavior of wasm programs (though we will also need to reach a similar level of trust on the interpreter)</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://peregrine-project.github.io/\">https://peregrine-project.github.io/</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I'm learning about this project now, as I understand their scope is to generate wasm rather than prove wasm, our goals is prove the behavior of wasm programs that were compiled from \"arbitrary\" sources (say rust, c++, etc...)</p>\n<p>A closer approach is iris, though that defined its own framework rather focusing on Wasm</p>",
        "id": 597060111,
        "sender_full_name": "Marcelo Fornet",
        "timestamp": 1779470835
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Really cool! Do you end up using mvcgen for this at all?</p>",
        "id": 597130234,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1779472846
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>3 messages were moved here from <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"579630\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/579630-Project-announcements/topic/Talos.3A.20A.20Formal.20Verification.20Framework.20for.20WebAssembly/with/597057652\">#Project announcements &gt; Talos: A Formal Verification Framework for WebAssembly</a> by <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110596\">Rob Lewis</span>.</p>",
        "id": 597136074,
        "sender_full_name": "Notification Bot",
        "timestamp": 1779474456
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>No, unfortunately. I’m exploring what are the possibilities there.</p>",
        "id": 597139709,
        "sender_full_name": "Marcelo Fornet",
        "timestamp": 1779475593
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"456449\">@Marcelo Fornet</span> Peregrine, based on certirocq-wasm, targets wasm from lean, rocq, cakeml and agda. The compiler as verified against the semantics of wasm.<br>\nThere is an iris version of wam-cert, partially build by my next door neighbor in Aarhus.<br>\nThere might be in interest in porting iris-wasm, as part of the iris port to lean.</p>",
        "id": 597151409,
        "sender_full_name": "Bas Spitters",
        "timestamp": 1779479309
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"456449\">Marcelo Fornet</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Talos.3A.20A.20Formal.20Verification.20Framework.20for.20WebAssembly/near/597060111\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>as I understand it the intention is to prove artifacts auto-generated from <a href=\"https://webassembly.org/news/2025-03-27-spectec/\">SpecTec</a>. </p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Once SpecTec has a working Lean backend, and thus a somewhat “official” Lean semantics, even if unwieldy, do you plan to connect to that (e.g. prove your semantics to be equivalent to theirs)?</p>",
        "id": 597342356,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1779571505
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>that would be ideal, otherwise our implementation is part of the \"source of trust\", and we rather offload the trust to the official spec.</p>",
        "id": 597342480,
        "sender_full_name": "Marcelo Fornet",
        "timestamp": 1779571643
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"721721\">Markus de Medeiros</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Talos.3A.20A.20Formal.20Verification.20Framework.20for.20WebAssembly/near/597130234\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Really cool! Do you end up using mvcgen for this at all?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I had a look. This is the definition of <code>wp</code>, I think: <a href=\"https://github.com/cajal-technologies/talos/blob/baa6f80f1b044b7cffad8c1ce89fa716bb408654/interpreter/Interpreter/Wasm/Wp/Defs.lean#L32\">https://github.com/cajal-technologies/talos/blob/baa6f80f1b044b7cffad8c1ce89fa716bb408654/interpreter/Interpreter/Wasm/Wp/Defs.lean#L32</a></p>\n<p>This is a deep embedding. The short answer is that using the current <code>mvcgen</code> in this scenario is not a good fit (= it is possible to extract a monadic interpreter <code>execM</code> from <code>exec</code>, but then you are really reasoning about <code>wp[[exec p]]</code>. Possible, but it might not be the most stable setup.). However, we are in the process of opening up the meta theory around <code>mvcgen</code> such that it is sufficient to implement a type class</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PredTrans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Pred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EPred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- Apply the predicate transformer to a postcondition and exception postcondition. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pred</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EPred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pred</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CompleteLattice</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">outParam</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Pred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">outParam</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">EPred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">outParam</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w'</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pred</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Assertion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EPred</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">wpTrans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PredTrans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EPred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">wp_trans_monotone</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wpTrans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;.</span><span class=\"n\">monotone</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and I'm optimistic that Talos' <code>wp</code> will be an instance of this type class, à la</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Program</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Locals</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Store</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">Fail</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">conditions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">all</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">except</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FallThrough</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">wpTrans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">post</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">epost</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">st</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fuel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≥</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fuel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">st</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FallThrough</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">st</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">post</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">st</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">all</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">other</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">epost</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;...&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">wp_trans_monotone</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- enjoy</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>When this new meta theory lands, we'll rename <code>mvcgen</code> to <code>vcgen</code> and declare victory :)</p>",
        "id": 597533187,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Graf",
        "timestamp": 1779715199
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for taking a look and provide this feedback. </p>\n<p>If I want to learn more about the internals of mvcgen, where do you recommend me to look at?</p>",
        "id": 597558092,
        "sender_full_name": "Marcelo Fornet",
        "timestamp": 1779726447
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So if you want to know how <code>mvcgen</code> can be used and how you can instantiate it with your framework, I suggest you check out the <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/commit/f3e3c0c7c2f4e20b85071f981197ad8c53910fb3\">tutorial</a> and the <a href=\"https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/latest/The--mvcgen--tactic/\">reference manual</a> (the material overlaps but you might prefer the top-down style of the tutorial to the more bottom-up style of the reference manual). If you want to know about the internals and the new implementation in terms of SymM in order to write your own VC generator, I suggest you check out <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/master/src/Lean/Elab/Tactic/Do/Internal/VCGen/Solve.lean\">https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/master/src/Lean/Elab/Tactic/Do/Internal/VCGen/Solve.lean</a>.</p>",
        "id": 597768894,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Graf",
        "timestamp": 1779784590
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"456449\">@Marcelo Fornet</span> <a href=\"https://github.com/logsem/iriswasm\">https://github.com/logsem/iriswasm</a> could readily be ported to iris-Lean. How would that compare to your work</p>",
        "id": 597811427,
        "sender_full_name": "Bas Spitters",
        "timestamp": 1779793026
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48584761\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48584761</a></p>",
        "id": 604525421,
        "sender_full_name": "Marcelo Fornet",
        "timestamp": 1781788672
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"259452\">Bas Spitters</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Talos.3A.20A.20Formal.20Verification.20Framework.20for.20WebAssembly/near/597811427\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"456449\">Marcelo Fornet</span> <a href=\"https://github.com/logsem/iriswasm\">https://github.com/logsem/iriswasm</a> could readily be ported to iris-Lean. How would that compare to your work</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The scope and target is very similar. I guess there are some foundational differences on how to verify code, for example we prove everything against an in interpreter, and have a thin wp-layer on top of it.</p>",
        "id": 604527360,
        "sender_full_name": "Marcelo Fornet",
        "timestamp": 1781789021
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/sgraf812/talos/blob/9875d3b4f9a17f9e93211ba20062bd3f78f045aa/wp/WasmWP/Basic.lean#L113\">Here</a> is a <code>WP</code> instance that adapts Talos to the upcoming <code>vcgen</code> in 4.35:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">U</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- TODO(flip): `Universal.State`, see the import note in the full listing</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- A Wasm program packaged with its execution context. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Code</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HostEnv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">U</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">prog</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Program</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Fuel-free weakest precondition of a `Code` against a continuation</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">predicate: some fuel bound suffices, and every larger fuel agrees. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Code</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Code</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Continuation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">U</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">st</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Store</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">U</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Locals</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fuel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≥</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">exec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fuel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">st</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prog</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Code</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EAssn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">wpTrans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">epost</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">contPost</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">())</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">epost</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">wp_trans_monotone</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">epost</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">epost'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hE</span><span class