class=\"n\">a'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">gcd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNat</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inv2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">params</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]!</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">asI32</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- termination variant</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">finish</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This is just a PoC that I guided Claude towards. It represents how I imagine <code>vcgen</code> be used. However, some of the low and medium-level design decisions might be questionable and well be answered differently. For example, I'm wary of the fact that Claude prefers to tuple up the <code>Program</code> with the module and host env instead of threading the latter through the assertion layer (like a ReaderT layer would).</p>",
        "id": 626077622,
